abstract: >-
  A speculative hypothesis treating the universe as a globally conserved
  informational structure, where cosmological cycles correspond to changes in
  local information readability rather than temporal restarts. Version 0.1.3
  tests a restricted finite Einstein-Cartan-inspired CAR selector. Its first
  three-cell extension fails boundary-independent robustness, while a four-cell
  matched non-axial onsite control reproduces the periodic small-twist branch.
  A bounded classification extends its residual law to every nonzero contact in
  the declared translation-invariant onsite quartic class. No EC-specific or
  derived cosmological transition is claimed.
